  "description": "Republic of Ireland District Electoral Divisions/Wards as at 1953-04-01, assembled from Connacht (= 1919 boundaries), Leinster 1953, Munster (= 1950 boundaries), Ulster (= 1921 boundaries). Modified version of District Electoral Divisions/Wards 1954. In 1954, following the expansion of Dublin county borough in 1953, 9 new wards replaced the portions of 9 DEDs (Castleknock, Clondalkin, Coolock, Drumcondra Rural, Finglas, Howth Rural, Palmerstown, Rathfarnham and Terenure) that had become part of the county borough. Minor boundary changes were made to some of the 33 existing wards (making a total of 42).",
